  "rules": [
    "This decomposes process 0. Parent external interface groups balance with the context DFD; PERSONAL_OUT is refined into access errors and feature-specific data/error results.",
    "Eight logical processes are responsibilities, not a selected service or deployment architecture. The per-story diagrams detail the data transformations and allowed writes.",
    "D2 maps to both preference relations; D4 maps to recipe, ingredient and step relations. D1 and D3-D7 map to their corresponding E-R entities.",
    "All protected input is authenticated and owner-scoped under process 8.0 (US-15). Every referenced object ID, including recipeId in a request body, is checked against the verified account before a read/write. Client owner IDs are rejected or ignored.",
    "Process 8.0 and each feature enforce owner-qualified access. Referenced IDs in path and body are both covered. The stores supply existence/ownership data, not client-chosen ownership."
  ]
